<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span><span id="S1.T2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Counterfactual demographic persona group <math id="S1.T2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{\text{Attribute}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">Attribute</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{\text{Attribute}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span> Each group varies by a specific demographic term (<math id="S1.T2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>) and includes corresponding persona templates (<math id="S1.T2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{w_{j}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{w_{j}}</annotation></semantics></math>) used in our analysis.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">2 </span>Uncovering Complementary Knowledge in Counterfactual Personas</h2>

<section id="S2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.1 </span>Simple Demographic Perturbation Impacts Performance</h3>

<div id="S2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To evaluate the model’s sensitivity to minor demographic cues embedded in persona prompts, we construct a set of counterfactual gender personas through the perturbing of demographic terms. Each group, <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{\text{Gender}}^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mtext>Gender</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{\text{Gender}}^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math>, contains three parallel personas, <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p^{(i)}_{\text{he}},p^{(i)}_{\text{she}},p^{(i)}_{\text{they}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mtext>he</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mtext>she</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mtext>they</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p^{(i)}_{\text{he}},p^{(i)}_{\text{she}},p^{(i)}_{\text{they}})</annotation></semantics></math>, that differ only in the pronouns <span id="S2.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">he</span>, <span id="S2.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">she</span>, and <span id="S2.SS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">they</span>. One base persona (e.g., <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{(i)}_{\text{he}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mtext>he</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{(i)}_{\text{he}}</annotation></semantics></math>) is randomly sampled from the PersonaHub dataset<span id="footnote1" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">1</span>
              
              
              
            <a href="https://huggingface.co/datasets/proj-persona/PersonaHub" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://huggingface.co/datasets/proj-persona/PersonaHub</a></span></span></span>, while the other two are created by systematically perturbing demographic terms (see Table <a href="#S1.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ CHOIR: Collaborative Harmonization fOr Inference Robustness" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>). This design ensures that all three personas share the same underlying identity and structure, differing only in their expressed demographic identity. We then use these persona groups to ask: <span id="S2.SS1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Are these gender-related expressions minor surface-level variations, or do they meaningfully influence the model’s reasoning path?</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#S0.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ CHOIR: Collaborative Harmonization fOr Inference Robustness" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> presents results for 15 personas, drawn from 5 groups where each group includes one base persona and its two counterfactual demographic variants (Table <a href="#S1.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ CHOIR: Collaborative Harmonization fOr Inference Robustness" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>), evaluated using the Llama-1B-Instruct model <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Touvron et al., 2023</a>)</cite> on the GSM8K dataset <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cobbe et al., 2021</a>)</cite>. Notably, even personas within the same group, differing only by surface-level demographic cues, often exhibit non-trivial performance gaps. In particular, in <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{\text{Gender}}^{(2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mtext>Gender</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{\text{Gender}}^{(2)}</annotation></semantics></math>, the persona <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{(2)}_{\text{she}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mtext>she</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{(2)}_{\text{she}}</annotation></semantics></math> achieves more than <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\%</annotation></semantics></math> higher accuracy than both <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{(2)}_{\text{he}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mtext>he</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{(2)}_{\text{he}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{(2)}_{\text{they}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mtext>they</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{(2)}_{\text{they}}</annotation></semantics></math>. <span id="S2.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">These findings indicate that even small demographic perturbations can influence reasoning performance.</span> While these results are reported for Llama, we observe qualitatively similar trends in other models, indicating that persona-induced variance is a general phenomenon across architectures, consistent with prior observations of persona-related bias <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gupta et al. (2024)</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.2 </span>Similar Accuracy, Divergent Reasoning</h3>

<div id="S2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Accuracy alone, however, does not capture the full picture. To probe deeper, we compare the sets of correctly answered questions across three persona pairs with nearly identical overall accuracies (Figure <a href="#S0.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ CHOIR: Collaborative Harmonization fOr Inference Robustness" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>):
(i) <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{(1)}_{\text{he}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mtext>he</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{(1)}_{\text{he}}</annotation></semantics></math> vs. <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{(1)}_{\text{she}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mtext>she</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{(1)}_{\text{she}}</annotation></semantics></math> (29.41% vs. 29.49%),
(ii) <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{(3)}_{\text{she}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mtext>she</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{(3)}_{\text{she}}</annotation></semantics></math> vs. <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{(3)}_{\text{they}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mtext>they</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{(3)}_{\text{they}}</annotation></semantics></math> (37.91% vs. 37.83%), and
(iii) <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{(4)}_{\text{he}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mtext>he</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{(4)}_{\text{he}}</annotation></semantics></math> vs. <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{(4)}_{\text{they}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mtext>they</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{(4)}_{\text{they}}</annotation></semantics></math> (39.80% vs. 39.73%).
We ask: <span id="S2.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Do these personas with similar overall accuracy actually solve the same set of questions correctly?</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#S1.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ CHOIR: Collaborative Harmonization fOr Inference Robustness" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> illustrates the pairwise overlaps and differences in correct-answer sets for each matched persona pair.
Surprisingly, even when the persona prompts differ only by a single pronoun, the distribution of correct answers can vary substantially.
For example, in <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{\text{Gender}}^{(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mtext>Gender</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{\text{Gender}}^{(1)}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{(1)}_{\text{he}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mtext>he</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{(1)}_{\text{he}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{(1)}_{\text{she}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mtext>she</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{(1)}_{\text{she}}</annotation></semantics></math> agree on 315 correct answers, yet each also shows distinct behavior: <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{(1)}_{\text{he}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mtext>he</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{(1)}_{\text{he}}</annotation></semantics></math> correctly answers 73 questions that <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{(1)}_{\text{she}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mtext>she</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{(1)}_{\text{she}}</annotation></semantics></math> does not, while <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{(1)}_{\text{she}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mtext>she</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{(1)}_{\text{she}}</annotation></semantics></math> solves 74 questions that <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{(1)}_{\text{he}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mtext>he</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{(1)}_{\text{he}}</annotation></semantics></math> misses. This results in over <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10\%</annotation></semantics></math> non-overlapping correct answers, despite only a <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.1\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.1</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.1\%</annotation></semantics></math> difference in overall accuracy. <span id="S2.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Such discrepancies reveal that even minor demographic perturbations can lead to meaningful divergences in reasoning outputs.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Takeaways.</span> Together, these findings indicate that even minimal demographic framing changes can alter the model’s behavior in meaningful ways. <span id="S2.SS2.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Motivated by this observation, we seek to exploit these variations constructively, allowing different persona demographic variants to complement one another and collectively improve reasoning consistency and robustness.</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span>CHOIR: Collaborative Harmonization fOr Inference Robustness</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.4.1" class="ltx_listingline">
<span id="alg1.4.1.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="alg1.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> </span>Question <math id="alg1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>; base persona <math id="alg1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>; persona instruction template <math id="alg1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>; language model <math id="alg1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>; max generation length <math id="alg1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="alg1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lambda}^{(0)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lambda}^{(0)}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="alg1.4.2" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="alg1.4.2.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="alg1.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span> </span>Answer <math id="alg1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="alg1.4.3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.4.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1</span></span>
            <span id="alg1.4.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// Step 1: Construct Counterfactual Personas</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.4.4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.4.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">2</span></span>
            Construct counterfactual personas <math id="alg1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{p_{2},\dots,p_{n}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p_{2},\dots,p_{n}\}</annotation></semantics></math> by modifying demographic attributes of <math id="alg1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="alg1.4.5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.4.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">3</span></span>
            Generate persona-specific instructions: <math id="alg1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}=T(p_{i}),\forall i\in\{1,\dots,n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}=T(p_{i}),\forall i\in\{1,\dots,n\}</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="alg1.4.6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.4.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">4</span></span>
            <span id="alg1.4.6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// Step 2: Dynamic Collaborative Decoding</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.4.7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.4.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">5</span></span>
            <span id="alg1.4.7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <em id="alg1.4.7.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">each generation step <math id="alg1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="alg1.4.7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.4.8" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.4.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">6</span></span>
            <span id="alg1.4.8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <em id="alg1.4.8.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">each persona <math id="alg1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> (including base and counterfactual personas)</em> <span id="alg1.4.8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.4.9" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.4.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">7</span></span>
            Compute logits and probabilities: <math id="alg1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}^{(i)}_{t}=f_{\theta}(r_{i},x,y_{&lt;t}),\mathbf{p}^{(i)}_{t}=\text{softmax}(\mathbf{z}^{(i)}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐩</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>softmax</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}^{(i)}_{t}=f_{\theta}(r_{i},x,y_{&lt;t}),\mathbf{p}^{(i)}_{t}=\text{softmax}(\mathbf{z}^{(i)}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="alg1.4.10" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.4.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">8</span></span>
            Compute confidence score: <math id="alg1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{(i)}_{t}=\max\mathbf{p}^{(i)}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐩</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{(i)}_{t}=\max\mathbf{p}^{(i)}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="alg1.4.11" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.4.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">9</span></span>
            Compute average consensus confidence: <math id="alg1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{s}_{t}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}s^{(i)}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{s}_{t}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}s^{(i)}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="alg1.4.12" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.4.12.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">10</span></span>
            <span id="alg1.4.12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <em id="alg1.4.12.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">each persona <math id="alg1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i},i\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i},i\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="alg1.4.12.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.4.13" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.4.13.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">11</span></span>
            <math id="alg1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{(i)}_{t}=|s^{(i)}_{t}-\bar{s}_{t}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{(i)}_{t}=|s^{(i)}_{t}-\bar{s}_{t}|</annotation></semantics></math> ;
</div>
<div id="alg1.4.14" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.4.14.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">12</span></span>
            <math id="alg1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha^{(i)}_{t}=1-d^{(i)}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha^{(i)}_{t}=1-d^{(i)}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> ;
</div>
<div id="alg1.4.15" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.4.15.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">13</span></span>
            Set <math id="alg1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha^{(0)}_{t}=\lambda^{(0)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha^{(0)}_{t}=\lambda^{(0)}</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="alg1.4.16" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.4.16.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">14</span></span>
            Compute base logits from pre-trained knowledge: <math id="alg1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}^{(0)}_{t}=f_{\theta}(x,y_{&lt;t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}^{(0)}_{t}=f_{\theta}(x,y_{&lt;t})</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="alg1.4.17" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.4.17.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">15</span></span>
            Aggregate logits: <math id="alg1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{\text{adj},t}=\sum_{i=0}^{n}\alpha^{(i)}_{t}\cdot\mathbf{z}^{(i)}_{t}=\alpha^{(0)}_{t}\cdot\mathbf{z}^{(0)}_{t}+\sum_{i=1}^{n}\alpha^{(i)}_{t}\cdot\mathbf{z}^{(i)}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mtext>adj</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{\text{adj},t}=\sum_{i=0}^{n}\alpha^{(i)}_{t}\cdot\mathbf{z}^{(i)}_{t}=\alpha^{(0)}_{t}\cdot\mathbf{z}^{(0)}_{t}+\sum_{i=1}^{n}\alpha^{(i)}_{t}\cdot\mathbf{z}^{(i)}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="alg1.4.18" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.4.18.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">16</span></span>
            Sample next token: <math id="alg1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{t}\sim\mathbf{p}_{\text{final},t}=\text{softmax}(\mathbf{z}_{\text{adj},t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>𝐩</mi><mrow><mtext>final</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>softmax</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mtext>adj</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{t}\sim\mathbf{p}_{\text{final},t}=\text{softmax}(\mathbf{z}_{\text{adj},t})</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="alg1.4.19" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.4.19.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">17</span></span>
            <span id="alg1.4.19.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <em id="alg1.4.19.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="alg1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is end-of-sequence token</em> <span id="alg1.4.19.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.4.20" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.4.20.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">18</span></span>
            <span id="alg1.4.20.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">break</span>;

</div>
<div id="alg1.4.21" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.4.21.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">19</span></span>
            <span id="alg1.4.21.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <em id="alg1.4.21.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="alg1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=\text{post\_processing}\{y_{1},\dots,y_{t}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">post_processing</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=\text{post\_processing}\{y_{1},\dots,y_{t}\}</annotation></semantics></math></em>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3 </span>CHOIR: Collaborative Harmonization fOr Inference Robustness</h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we introduce CHOIR (Collaborative Harmonization fOr Inference Robustness), a framework that strengthens the robustness and reliability of persona-assigned LLMs in reasoning tasks. By systematically constructing counterfactual personas and harmonizing their outputs during inference, CHOIR leverages demographic variation as a source of complementary reasoning rather than noise. The method consists of two key stages: Counterfactual Persona Construction and Dynamic Collaborative Decoding.</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.1 </span>Counterfactual Persona Construction</h3>

<div id="S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The first stage introduces diversity into reasoning by generating counterfactual personas.
Starting from a base persona <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> randomly sampled from the PersonaHub dataset, CHOIR constructs alternative counterfactual personas <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{p_{2},\dots,p_{n}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p_{2},\dots,p_{n}\}</annotation></semantics></math> by modifying the demographic attributes of <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, such as gender pronouns or religious identifiers (Table <a href="#S1.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ CHOIR: Collaborative Harmonization fOr Inference Robustness" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>). These perturbations preserve the underlying identity and task-relevant knowledge while altering surface-level demographic framing.
Each persona <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is then embedded into an instruction template <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> (Table <a href="#A2.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ B.2 Prompting Details ‣ Appendix B More Implementation Details ‣ CHOIR: Collaborative Harmonization fOr Inference Robustness" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>), producing persona-conditioned prompts: <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}=T(p_{i}),\forall i\in\{1,\dots,n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}=T(p_{i}),\forall i\in\{1,\dots,n\}</annotation></semantics></math>. This process yields a set of parallel reasoning prompts, each representing a distinct demographic lens.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2 </span>Dynamic Collaborative Decoding</h3>

<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Once the persona instructions <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{r_{1},\dots,r_{n}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{r_{1},\dots,r_{n}\}</annotation></semantics></math> are established, CHOIR performs multi-step collaborative inference by harmonizing token-level predictions across personas. The key idea is to first aggregate reasoning signals from all personas and then measure how each individual persona diverges from this collective consensus to determine its stability and contribution.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">At each generation step <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, the LLM <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> processes each persona instruction <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, the input question <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, the Zero-shot Chain-of-Thought trigger “Let’s think step by step” <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kojima et al., 2022</a>)</cite>, and the previously generated tokens <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{&lt;t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{&lt;t}</annotation></semantics></math>, producing persona-conditioned logits and probabilities:</p>
<table id="S3.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}^{(i)}_{t}=f_{\theta}(r_{i},x,y_{&lt;t}),\quad\mathbf{p}^{(i)}_{t}=\text{softmax}(\mathbf{z}^{(i)}_{t})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐩</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>softmax</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}^{(i)}_{t}=f_{\theta}(r_{i},x,y_{&lt;t}),\quad\mathbf{p}^{(i)}_{t}=\text{softmax}(\mathbf{z}^{(i)}_{t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Following previous work <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Geng et al. (2024)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kumar et al. (2024)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al. (2025)</a></cite>, we define the confidence of persona <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> as the maximum token probability: <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{(i)}_{t}=\max\mathbf{p}^{(i)}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐩</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{(i)}_{t}=\max\mathbf{p}^{(i)}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Consensus confidence and divergence.</span> To measure agreement and disagreement across personas, we first compute the average confidence across all personas: <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{s}_{t}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}s^{(i)}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{s}_{t}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}s^{(i)}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, and measure each persona’s divergence from this consensus: <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{(i)}_{t}=\big|s^{(i)}_{t}-\bar{s}_{t}\big|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{(i)}_{t}=\big|s^{(i)}_{t}-\bar{s}_{t}\big|</annotation></semantics></math>.
These differences serve as a proxy for uncertainty in the model’s behavior under different demographic perspectives.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Dynamic weighting and aggregation.</span>
Next, we assign each persona a dynamic weight based on its consistency with the consensus confidence. The intuition is that small demographic perturbations should not substantially alter the reasoning path: personas that remain close to the collective average are more stable and reliable, whereas those that diverge significantly are less robust. Accordingly, each persona <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is assigned a weight that decreases with its divergence from the average confidence:</p>
<table id="S3.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}^{(i)}=\begin{cases}\lambda^{(0)},&amp;i=0\\
\lambda^{(i)}-d^{(i)}_{t},&amp;i\geq 1.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}^{(i)}=\begin{cases}\lambda^{(0)},&amp;i=0\\
\lambda^{(i)}-d^{(i)}_{t},&amp;i\geq 1.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p4.3" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> is a knowledge weight hyperparameter and <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=0</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to the non-persona baseline, representing the model’s internal pretrained reasoning priors without any demographic influence. The base logits without persona influence are computed as <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}^{(0)}_{t}=f_{\theta}(x,y_{&lt;t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}^{(0)}_{t}=f_{\theta}(x,y_{&lt;t})</annotation></semantics></math>. The specific values chosen for <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> in our experiments are detailed in §<a href="#S4" title="4 Experimental Setup ‣ CHOIR: Collaborative Harmonization fOr Inference Robustness" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, with a more in-depth analysis of <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda^{(0)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{(0)}</annotation></semantics></math> provided in §<a href="#S5.SS3" title="5.3 RQ3: What are the key components driving CHOIR’s success? ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ CHOIR: Collaborative Harmonization fOr Inference Robustness" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a>.
The adjusted logits are obtained as a weighted sum of persona-specific and base logits:</p>
<table id="S3.E3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E3X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E3X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{z}_{\text{adj},t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mtext>adj</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{z}_{\text{adj},t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E3X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=0}^{n}\alpha^{(i)}_{t}\cdot\mathbf{z}^{(i)}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=0}^{n}\alpha^{(i)}_{t}\cdot\mathbf{z}^{(i)}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E3Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E3Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\alpha^{(0)}_{t}\cdot\underbrace{\mathbf{z}_{t}^{(0)}}_{\raisebox{-2.3917pt}{$\mathclap{\shortstack{\text{Pretrained}\\
 \text{Knowledge}}}$}}+\alpha^{(1)}_{t}\cdot\underbrace{\mathbf{z}_{t}^{(1)}}_{\raisebox{-2.3917pt}{$\mathclap{\shortstack{\text{Base}\\
 \text{Persona}}}$}}+\sum_{i=2}^{n}\alpha^{(i)}_{t}\cdot\underbrace{\mathbf{z}_{t}^{(i)}}_{\raisebox{-2.3917pt}{$\mathclap{\shortstack{\text{Counterfactual}\\
 \text{Personas}}}$}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mpadded style="width:0pt;" lspace="-20.2pt" voffset="-2.4pt" width="0pt"><mtext>
<span class="ltx_inline-block"> 
<span class="ltx_p"><span class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">Pretrained</span></span> 
<span class="ltx_p"><span class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">Knowledge</span></span> 
</span></mtext></mpadded></munder></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mpadded style="width:0pt;" lspace="-15.0pt" voffset="-2.4pt" width="0pt"><mtext>
<span class="ltx_inline-block"> 
<span class="ltx_p"><span class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">Base</span></span> 
<span class="ltx_p"><span class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">Persona</span></span> 
</span></mtext></mpadded></munder></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mpadded style="width:0pt;" lspace="-26.0pt" voffset="-2.4pt" width="0pt"><mtext>
<span class="ltx_inline-block"> 
<span class="ltx_p"><span class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">Counterfactual</span></span> 
<span class="ltx_p"><span class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">Personas</span></span> 
</span></mtext></mpadded></munder></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\alpha^{(0)}_{t}\cdot\underbrace{\mathbf{z}_{t}^{(0)}}_{\raisebox{-2.3917pt}{$\mathclap{\shortstack{\text{Pretrained}\\
 \text{Knowledge}}}$}}+\alpha^{(1)}_{t}\cdot\underbrace{\mathbf{z}_{t}^{(1)}}_{\raisebox{-2.3917pt}{$\mathclap{\shortstack{\text{Base}\\
 \text{Persona}}}$}}+\sum_{i=2}^{n}\alpha^{(i)}_{t}\cdot\underbrace{\mathbf{z}_{t}^{(i)}}_{\raisebox{-2.3917pt}{$\mathclap{\shortstack{\text{Counterfactual}\\
 \text{Personas}}}$}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p4.4" class="ltx_p">The final token distribution is computed via softmax: <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{p}_{\text{final},t}=\text{\text{softmax}}(\mathbf{z}_{\text{adj},t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐩</mi><mrow><mtext>final</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>softmax</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mtext>adj</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{p}_{\text{final},t}=\text{\text{softmax}}(\mathbf{z}_{\text{adj},t})</annotation></semantics></math>, from which the next token <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is sampled. The decoding process continues iteratively until an end-of-sequence token is generated. Once the complete sequence <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=\{y_{1},y_{2},\dots,y_{t}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=\{y_{1},y_{2},\dots,y_{t}\}</annotation></semantics></math> is generated, CHOIR applies post-processing to extract the final answer <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kong et al., 2024b</a>)</cite>. The full process is summarized in Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="In 2.2 Similar Accuracy, Divergent Reasoning ‣ 2 Uncovering Complementary Knowledge in Counterfactual Personas ‣ CHOIR: Collaborative Harmonization fOr Inference Robustness" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Experimental Setup</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Tasks, datasets, and models.</span>
We evaluate CHOIR on arithmetic reasoning tasks: GSM8K <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cobbe et al., 2021</a>)</cite>, SingleEq <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Koncel-Kedziorski et al., 2015</a>)</cite>, and MultiArith <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Roy and Roth, 2015</a>)</cite>, and the commonsense reasoning task: CSQA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Talmor et al., 2019</a>)</cite>. Detailed dataset statistics are provided in Appendix <a href="#A2.SS1" title="B.1 Dataset and Model Details ‣ Appendix B More Implementation Details ‣ CHOIR: Collaborative Harmonization fOr Inference Robustness" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>. Our experiments are conducted on several open-source instruction-tuned models at varying scales, including Llama 3-Instruct series (1B, 3B, 8B) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Touvron et al., 2023</a>)</cite>, Qwen 2.5-Instruct (1.5B, 3B, 7B) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Qwen Team, 2024</a>)</cite>, and Mistral-Instruct (8B) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mistral AI, 2024</a>)</cite>.<span id="footnote2" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup>
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">2</span>
            
            
            
          Due to OpenAI API restrictions on logits (limited to the top-20 tokens), we cannot obtain full-vocabulary logits for API-based models. Exploring methods compatible with these restrictions is left for future work.</span></span></span></p>
</div>
