roke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -9.96 18.38)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 51.51)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 8.61)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#0000FF;--ltx-fill-color:#0000FF;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#0000FF" stroke="#0000FF" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(0.28,0)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 11.81 0 L 23.62 0"></path><path d="M 14.58 0 C 14.58 1.53 13.34 2.77 11.81 2.77 C 10.28 2.77 9.04 1.53 9.04 0 C 9.04 -1.53 10.28 -2.77 11.81 -2.77 C 13.34 -2.77 14.58 -1.53 14.58 0 Z M 11.81 0"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 27.02 0) translate(32.36,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -29.6 -3.77)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:4.28em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="59.19"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S5.F4.pic1.8" class="ltx_text">Llama-8B</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 25.75)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FF0000;--ltx-fill-color:#FF0000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#FF0000" stroke="#FF0000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(0.28,0)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 11.81 0 L 23.62 0"></path><path d="M 9.04 -2.77 h 5.53 v 5.53 h -5.53 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 28.85 0) translate(30.54,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -27.77 -3.69)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:4.04em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.15" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="55.93"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S5.F4.pic1.9" class="ltx_text">Qwen-7B</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 42.9)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#009900;--ltx-fill-color:#009900;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#009900" stroke="#009900" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(0.28,0)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 11.81 0 L 23.62 0"></path><path d="M 11.81 2.77 L 14.21 -1.38 L 9.41 -1.38 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 24.18 0) translate(35.21,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -32.44 -3.77)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:4.69em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="64.88"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S5.F4.pic1.10" class="ltx_text">Mistral-8B</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g></g></g></g></svg></span>
</span></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 4: </span><span id="S5.F4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Analysis of the pre-trained knowledge weight <math id="S5.F4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda^{(0)}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{(0)}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> on GSM8K (Gender).</span> Results reveal a model-specific optimal balance, indicating that different architectures have varying reliance on their base priors.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Structured Perturbations are Better than Random Ones:</span> The way diversity is generated matters. Using our structured, demographically counterfactual personas is more effective than using randomly selected personas from PersonaHub (CHOIR w/ Random Personas) (82.1% vs. 80.3%), indicating that CHOIR’s controlled, minimal perturbation approach generates more meaningful and complementary reasoning signals.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Balancing Personas with Base Knowledge is Critical:</span> The model’s pre-trained knowledge is vital for grounding the reasoning process. Completely removing the influence of the base model (wo/ Pre-trained Knowledge) causes a significant drop in accuracy from 82.1% to 79.3%. While our main experiments use a fixed heuristic <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda^{(0)}=n-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{(0)}=n-1</annotation></semantics></math> and achieve significantly improved performance, we conducted a follow-up analysis to investigate the optimal setting for this key hyperparameter across different model architectures by setting the weight range from 0 to 4. As shown in Figure <a href="#S5.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ 5.3 RQ3: What are the key components driving CHOIR’s success? ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ CHOIR: Collaborative Harmonization fOr Inference Robustness" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, we find that the optimal balance is model-specific. While Llama-8B confirms that <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda^{(0)}=n-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{(0)}=n-1</annotation></semantics></math> is optimal (82.11%), Qwen-7B peaks at a weight of 1 (66.19%), and Mistral-8B’s performance is highest at a weight of 4 (86.05%). This indicates that <span id="S5.SS3.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">different model families have varying reliance on their base knowledge</span>. This finding indicates that while CHOIR is highly effective with a default setting, its performance can be further maximized by tuning this hyperparameter.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.F5" class="ltx_figure">
<div id="S5.F5.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:241.5pt;height:186.9pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(0.4pt,-0.3pt) scale(1.00332996351608,1.00332996351608) ;"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S5.F5.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="257.76" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 323.83 257.76" width="323.83"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,257.76) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(46.68,0) translate(0,27.55) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -46.68 -27.55)"><g class="ltx_nestedsvg" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 0) translate(97.27,0) translate(0,27.55)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#808080;--ltx-fill-color:#808080;--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" color="#808080" fill="#808080" stroke="#808080" stroke-width="0.2pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 -5.91 L 0 0 M 168.64 -5.91 L 168.64 0 M 0 230.07 L 0 224.17 M 168.64 230.07 L 168.64 224.17"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#808080;--ltx-fill-color:#808080;--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" color="#808080" fill="#808080" stroke="#808080" stroke-width="0.2pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -50.59 0 L -44.69 0 M -50.59 68.97 L -44.69 68.97 M -50.59 137.95 L -44.69 137.95 M -50.59 206.92 L -44.69 206.92 M 219.23 0 L 213.32 0 M 219.23 68.97 L 213.32 68.97 M 219.23 137.95 L 213.32 137.95 M 219.23 206.92 L 213.32 206.92"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -50.59 0 L -50.59 224.17 L 219.23 224.17 L 219.23 0 L -50.59 0 Z"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -24.46 -20.25)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.53em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.46" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="48.91"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S5.F5.pic1.1" class="ltx_text">GSM8K</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 115.33 -20.25)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:7.71em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.15" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="106.62"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S5.F5.pic1.2" class="ltx_text">CommonsenseQA</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -62.4 -4.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.64em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.92" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.92)" width="6.92"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.F5.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -69.32 64.52)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1em;--ltx-fo-height:0.64em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.92" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.92)" width="13.84"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.F5.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>20</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">20</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -69.32 133.49)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1em;--ltx-fo-height:0.64em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.92" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.92)" width="13.84"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.F5.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="40" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>40</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">40</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -69.32 202.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1em;--ltx-fo-height:0.64em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.92" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.92)" width="13.84"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.F5.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="60" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>60</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">60</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><clipPath id="pgfcp6"><path d="M -50.59 0 L 219.23 0 L 219.23 224.17 L -50.59 224.17 Z"></path></clipPath><g clip-path="url(#pgfcp6)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#4D4DFF;" fill="#4D4DFF"><path d="M -17.99 0 h 16.6 v 76.22 h -16.6 Z M 150.65 0 h 16.6 v 118.98 h -16.6 Z"></path></g><g></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFA64D;" fill="#FFA64D"><path d="M 1.38 0 h 16.6 v 150.36 h -16.6 Z M 170.02 0 h 16.6 v 197.95 h -16.6 Z"></path></g><g></g></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -23.14 81.1)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.94em;--ltx-fo-height:0.64em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.92" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.92)" width="26.91"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.F5.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="22.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>22.1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">22.1</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 145.5 123.87)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.94em;--ltx-fo-height:0.64em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.92" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.92)" width="26.91"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.F5.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="34.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>34.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">34.5</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -3.77 155.25)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.94em;--ltx-fo-height:0.64em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.92" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.92)" width="26.91"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.F5.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="43.6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>43.6</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">43.6</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 164.87 202.84)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.94em;--ltx-fo-height:0.64em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.92" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.92)" width="26.91"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.F5.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="57.4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>57.4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">57.4</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(0.0 1.0 -1.0 0.0 -82.28 70.55)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:6em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="83.06"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S5.F5.pic1.3" class="ltx_text">Accuracy (%)</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" stroke="#000000"><path d="M -42.22 176.53 h 110.83 v 40.63 h -110.83 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -38.07 187.83)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 35.1)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 8.99)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#4D4DFF;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#4D4DFF" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(2.35,0)"><path d="M -2.08 -2.77 h 4.15 v 11.07 h -4.15 Z M 6.23 -2.77 h 4.15 v 8.3 h -4.15 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 24.44 0) translate(33.32,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -30.56 -4.15)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:4.42em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="61.11"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S5.F5.pic1.4" class="ltx_text">SC (N=3)</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 26.57)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFA64D;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#FFA64D" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(2.35,0)"><path d="M -2.08 -2.77 h 4.15 v 11.07 h -4.15 Z M 6.23 -2.77 h 4.15 v 8.3 h -4.15 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 13.01 0) translate(44.76,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -41.99 -3.69)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:6.07em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.08em;font-size:10pt;" height="10.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="83.98"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S5.F5.pic1.5" class="ltx_text">CHOIR + SC</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g></g></g></g></svg></span>
</span></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 5: </span><span id="S5.F5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CHOIR + Self-Consistency (SC) vs. SC baseline on GSM8K and CommonsenseQA (Llama-8B, Gender).</span> Integrating SC reasoning with CHOIR improves accuracy across both datasets.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.4 </span>RQ4: Can CHOIR enhance other ensemble methods?</h3>

<div id="S5.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To test the generality of our harmonization mechanism, we applied it to the noisy reasoning paths generated by Self-Consistency (SC). As shown in Figure <a href="#S5.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ 5.3 RQ3: What are the key components driving CHOIR’s success? ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ CHOIR: Collaborative Harmonization fOr Inference Robustness" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, standard SC performs poorly with only three paths, achieving just 22.1% accuracy. By applying CHOIR’s dynamic weighting to these same paths, performance dramatically improves to 43.6%. This indicates that CHOIR is feasible for integration with existing methods, though it achieves its full potential when the paths are generated from controlled, meaningful perturbations rather than purely stochastic sampling.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">6 </span>Related Work</h2>

<section id="S6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.1 </span>LLM Reasoning</h3>

<div id="S6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">LLMs with parameters beyond a certain scale exhibit emergent reasoning abilities <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wei et al., 2022</a>; <a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cobbe et al., 2021</a>)</cite>. When provided with examples of “chain of thought” (CoT), which represent intermediate natural language reasoning steps, these models can generate explicit rationales similar to eliciting inductive/abductive reasoning <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wei et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Huang and Chang, 2023</a>)</cite>. Advances such as zero-shot CoT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kojima et al., 2022</a>)</cite>, where a model is prompted with phrases like “Let’s think step by step,” allow for reasoning without the need for explicit few-shot examples. Building on this, multi-step reasoning approaches – such as Successive Prompting <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dua et al., 2022</a>)</cite>, Tree-of-Thought <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yao et al., 2023a</a>)</cite>, Graph-of-Thought <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Besta et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yao et al., 2023b</a>)</cite>, Iterating CoT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2022a</a>)</cite>, and Self-Consistency <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2022b</a>)</cite> – have become critical strategies for enhancing reasoning in various downstream tasks. Many recent research works have been focused on improving the LLM Reasoning abilities as a pre-training or post-training effort. DeepSeek-R1 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">DeepSeek-AI, 2025</a>)</cite> is a notable stride forward in the direction of open-source reasoning model trained via large-scale reinforcement learning (RL) without supervised fine-tuning (SFT). There have also been some work in the direction of latent reasoning to scale up the test-time compute via implicitly reasoning in latent space through recurrent depth <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xu et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Geiping et al., 2025</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.2 </span>Persona-assigned LLM</h3>

<div id="S6.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Persona assignment in large language models (LLMs) refers to giving the model a specific role or identity (e.g. “You are a math teacher”) during prompting. This technique, also called <span id="S6.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">role prompting</span> or <span id="S6.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">role-play</span>, has gained popularity as a way to steer LLM behavior in desirable ways. By adopting a persona, an LLM can generate more in-character responses tailored to that role which in turn found to improve the zero-shot reasoning capabilities <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kong et al., 2024a</a>)</cite>. Coupling a persona with an LLM can activate the model’s corresponding parametric knowledge and style, enabling it to produce responses aligned with that role <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tseng et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dong et al., 2025</a>)</cite>. Adopting expert personas, especially aligned with the task domain, has demonstrated improved accuracy on mathematical reasoning benchmarks like GSM8K and AQuA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Luo et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhao et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. Persona prompts naturally elicit detailed reasoning traces, thereby enhancing inductive, deductive, and multi-step logical reasoning <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kong et al., 2024a</a>; <a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">He et al., 2023</a>)</cite>. However, inappropriate personas may degrade reasoning performance by introducing extraneous or misleading context. Large-scale studies have shown persona effects to be highly variable, indicating no guaranteed improvements <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zheng et al. (2024)</a></cite>. Further, personas might amplify biases and produce unsafe outputs, underscoring the need for cautious implementation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhao et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zheng et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gupta et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tan and Lee, 2025</a>)</cite>. To mitigate biases introduced by personas in LLM reasoning, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kim et al. (2024)</a></cite> propose ensemble prompting, combining persona-driven responses with neutral prompts and selecting the most accurate output through automated evaluation.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S7" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">7 </span>Conclusion</h2>

<div id="S7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We reframe persona-induced variance as a source of complementary reasoning rather than bias and introduce CHOIR, a test-time framework that harnesses this diversity to improve performance. Future work includes exploring advanced fusion mechanisms, such as attention-based or learnable weighting, to better integrate reasoning signals.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Sx1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section">Limitations</h2>

<div id="Sx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The current implementation of CHOIR requires full access to the model’s output logits to perform dynamic weighting. This restricts its use to open-source or full-access models. This presents a compelling direction for future research: developing “logit-free” harmonization techniques that can approximate CHOIR’s dynamic weighting using only top-k probabilities from restricted APIs. This would extend the benefits of collaborative decoding to a wider range of models.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Sx2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section">Ethical Consideration</h2>

<div id="Sx2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our work operates at the intersection of model reasoning and demographic representation. Our use of demographic terms (e.g., race, gender) is as minimal semantic probes to generate cognitive diversity in the model’s reasoning process. A potential risk is that CHOIR, while improving final accuracy, relies on the model’s underlying sensitivities to these terms, which may themselves stem from societal biases present in the training data. A primary finding and positive ethical outcome of our work is that CHOIR mitigates performance disparities across different demographic framings. For instance, by improving performance on personas that are otherwise disadvantaged (e.g., the “disabled” persona), CHOIR leads to more equitable and reliable model behavior. Instead of amplifying biases, our method harmonizes differences to produce a more robust and stable result that is less sensitive to any single demographic term. As with any technology involving persona assignment, we advocate for its responsible application and further research into its societal impact.</p>
</div>
</section>
