<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>More Results and Analysis</h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Detailed Performance Analysis by Persona Group</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As shown in Table <a href="#A3.T10" title="Table 10 ‣ C.1 Detailed Performance Analysis by Persona Group ‣ Appendix C More Results and Analysis ‣ CHOIR: Collaborative Harmonization fOr Inference Robustness" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>, the quality of the initial persona influences both baseline performance and the degree of improvement under CHOIR. For instance, G(1) starts with the lowest base accuracy (<math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>&lt;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;</annotation></semantics></math>30%) but sees the largest improvement (+9%), while the Expert persona starts strong (<math id="A3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim</annotation></semantics></math>41%) and improves modestly to 43%. Despite starting from a lower point, G(1) surpasses G(5) after CHOIR, showing that weaker personas benefit more, while stronger personas still improve. Moreover, a key outcome of the harmonization is that it brings all persona groups into a similar, high-performing range (39 - 43%), effectively reducing variance across personas. This illustrates its robustness and its advantage over static persona prompting by mitigating reliance on any single, potentially misaligned persona.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T10" class="ltx_table">
<div id="A3.T10.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:119.8pt;vertical-align:-58.7pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-174.9pt,60.7pt) scale(0.496610353284057,0.496610353284057) ;">
