</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Robustness to the Choice of Demographic Attributes</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To test CHOIR’s robustness to the specific composition of the demographic terms, we compared our primary “Race 1” configuration (three attributes: White, Black, Asian) against a “Race 2” configuration (four attributes: White, Black, Asian, Hispanic). As shown in Figure <a href="#A5.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ Appendix E Robustness to the Choice of Demographic Attributes ‣ CHOIR: Collaborative Harmonization fOr Inference Robustness" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, the performance is highly stable across both sets. This confirms that CHOIR is not overly sensitive to the specific choice or number of demographic attributes used.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.F6" class="ltx_figure">
<div id="A5.F6.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:77.2pt;vertical-align:-37.7pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-321.4pt,71.9pt) scale(0.349285338196301,0.349285338196301) ;">
