bject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(0.0 1.0 -1.0 0.0 -89.2 70.55)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:6em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="83.06"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A5.F6.pic4.5" class="ltx_text">Accuracy (%)</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 31.01 240.04)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:7.71em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.15" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="106.62"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A5.F6.pic4.6" class="ltx_text">CommonsenseQA</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g></svg></span></td></tr>
</table>
</span></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6: </span>Accuracy comparison on four reasoning datasets. Blue bars represent Race 1 scores and orange bars represent Race 2 scores across three models (Llama-8B, Qwen-7B, Mistral-8B).</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Case Study</h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A6.T13" title="Table 13 ‣ Appendix F Case Study ‣ CHOIR: Collaborative Harmonization fOr Inference Robustness" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a> shows that different demographic personas produce different reasoning paths, leading to different answers, making it difficult to reach a consensus through simple majority voting.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A6.T13" class="ltx_table">
<div id="A6.T13.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:341.6pt;height:252.8pt;vertical-align:-124.3pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-33.3pt,24.6pt) scale(0.8369068841593,0.8369068841593) ;">
<table id="A6.T13.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A6.T13.2.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A6.T13.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_tt">
<span id="A6.T13.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:42.7pt;">
<span id="A6.T13.2.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">Question</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A6.T13.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_tt">
<span id="A6.T13.2.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:341.4pt;">
<span id="A6.T13.2.1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">A hand-painted wallpaper costs $400 at the market. A DIY will saves 20% after considering the materials cost. If Ethan made his own hand-painted wallpaper, how much was the total cost?</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T13.2.1.2" class="ltx_tr" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;">
<td id="A6.T13.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="A6.T13.2.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:42.7pt;--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;">
<span id="A6.T13.2.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">Persona 1</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A6.T13.2.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="A6.T13.2.1.2.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:341.4pt;--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;">
<span id="A6.T13.2.1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">First, we need to calculate the 20% savings on the $400 wallpaper. That’s 20/100 * $400 = $80. So, the cost of the materials would be $400 - $80 = $320. Now, if Ethan made his own hand-painted wallpaper, he would save the $80 he would have spent on the wallpaper itself. So, the total cost for Ethan would be the materials cost plus the savings, which is $320 + $80 = <span id="A6.T13.2.1.2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">$400</span>.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T13.2.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A6.T13.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="A6.T13.2.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:42.7pt;">
<span id="A6.T13.2.1.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">Persona 2</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A6.T13.2.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="A6.T13.2.1.3.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:341.4pt;">
<span id="A6.T13.2.1.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">First, we need to calculate the savings on the wallpaper if Ethan makes it himself. The savings are 20% of $400, which is $400 * 0.20 = $80. Now, we subtract the savings from the original price to find the cost of the DIY wallpaper. So, $400 - $80 = $320. That’s the cost of the materials. But we also need to consider the time and effort Ethan puts in, which is priceless. So, the total cost for Ethan making his own hand-painted wallpaper is <span id="A6.T13.2.1.3.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#00FF00;">$320</span>.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T13.2.1.4" class="ltx_tr" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;">
<td id="A6.T13.2.1.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb">
<span id="A6.T13.2.1.4.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:42.7pt;--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;">
<span id="A6.T13.2.1.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">Persona 3</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A6.T13.2.1.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb">
<span id="A6.T13.2.1.4.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:341.4pt;--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;">
<span id="A6.T13.2.1.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">First, we need to calculate the savings on the wallpaper itself. If the wallpaper costs $400 and DIY saves 20%, then the savings would be 20% of $400. That’s $400 * 0.20 = $80. So, the cost of the wallpaper after the savings would be $400 - $80 = $320. Now, we need to consider the cost of materials. If DIY saves 20% on the wallpaper, it means the materials cost is 80% of the original price. So, the materials cost would be $400 * 0.80 = $320. Therefore, the total cost for Ethan to make his own hand-painted wallpaper would be the cost of the wallpaper after savings plus the cost of materials, which is $320 + $320 = <span id="A6.T13.2.1.4.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">$640</span>.</span>
</span></td></tr>
</table>
</span></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 13: </span>Case study.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</article>
